{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790346892,"nonce":"71YdLO4zU5FtWLTwo86uD7733Uc=","title":"CompilationConfig defaults to a placeholder ARC pass","message":"CompilationConfig::default() sets `memory_strategy: Some(MemoryStrategy::ARC)`, and compile_to_hir runs MemoryManagementPass whenever a strategy is set. ARCManager (crates/compiler/src/memory_management.rs) inserts a retain before every use of a pointer-typed value and a release right after its definition, with no last-use tracking; Cranelift lowers these to a count in the pointee's first word with a free at zero. The production runtimes lower through LoweringContext and never run this pass, but InterpRuntime::compile_typed_program (zyntax_embed), zyntax_wasm and compile_to_jit take the default.\n\nThe default should be no strategy or the drop-site analysis, and the ARC scaffold should be finished or removed.","files":null}]}